      "verificationNote": "Read directly from the UnitedHealthcare 2026 PDL, effective January 1, 2026, pages 19-20 (Cardiovascular section covering antihypertensives). Confirmed: 'lisinopril oral 1', 'lisinopril-hydrochlorothiazide 1', 'benazepril hcl oral 1', 'benazepril-hydrochlorothiazide 1' (page 19), 'captopril oral 1' (page 19), 'enalapril maleate oral tablet 1', 'enalapril maleate oral solution 3 PA', 'enalapril-hydrochlorothiazide 1', 'fosinopril sodium 1' (page 20) -- all generic ACE inhibitors are Tier 1 with no PA except the enalapril oral solution liquid formulation, which is Tier 3 PA. No brand-name ACE inhibitor (e.g., Zestril, Prinivil, Vasotec, Lotensin) is separately listed as still marketed/covered -- LOTENSIN and LOTENSIN HCT appear on page 20 at Tier 4 (brand benazepril), confirming brand is non-preferred versus generic. Ramipril was searched for but not found as a distinct line item in the pages read; the class as a whole is generically dominated at Tier 1 per the PDL's generic medication policy (page 5). [Reused: same national UHC commercial PDL as the MD guide (2026-10-21); outside CT/NJ/NY its 'E' symbol means may be excluded]",
